  "note": "Election of the Dromore Urban Council, January 1926. After withdrawals seven candidates remained for nine seats, so all were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1926, p. 7). Eight retiring members were among the ten nominated. The withdrawals were F. R. Hamilton, Alex. Mills and James M'Crea; two seats were left to be filled by co-option. Returned unopposed."
